          "sourceField": "destination",
          "sourceQuote": {
            "kind": "court",
            "name": "Civil division of the Missouri circuit court in the county of arrest",
            "detail": "Filed with the clerk of the circuit court, civil division, for the county where the arrest occurred. The clerk then does three things the printed instructions on CR145 set out: issues a copy of the petition to the prosecuting attorney; sends a copy of the petition and the fingerprint card to the Missouri Criminal Record Repository at the Highway Patrol; and gives notice of the hearing to the prosecuting attorney and to each official, agency or other entity named in the petition. The court sets the hearing no sooner than thirty days from filing."
