          "actual": "Instructions say circuit court in the county of arrest but omit its civil division.",
          "repair": "Name the civil division of the circuit court in the arrest county."
        },
        {
          "id": "MO610-HEARING-MINIMUM",
          "obligation": "SERVICE",
          "fixtures": [
            "canonical",
            "boundary",
            "petition-only"
          ],
          "sourceField": "rules.notice",
          "sourceQuote": "The court sets a hearing no sooner than thirty days from the filing of the petition and gives reasonable notice of the hearing to each official, agency or other entity named in the petition (\u00a7 610.123.3). CR145's printed instructions to the clerk add that a copy of the petition is issued to the prosecuting attorney and that a copy of the petition and the fingerprint card is sent to the Missouri Criminal Record Repository.",
          "actual": "Instructions correctly assign clerk notice but omit the no-sooner-than-30-days-from-filing hearing requirement.",
          "repair": "State the court sets hearing no sooner than thirty days from filing and gives reasonable notice; preserve actual-court-notice instruction."
        },
        {
          "id": "MO610-PROCUREMENT-CHECKLIST",
          "obligation": "REQUIRED_BEFORE_FILING",
          "fixtures": [
            "canonical",
            "boundary",
            "petition-only"
          ],
          "sourceField": "packetSet.participantActionRequired / requiredBeforeFiling",
          "sourceQuote": [
            "Obtain Three standard fingerprint cards. Ring a local police department or sheriff's office and ask whether they take fingerprint impressions on standard cards for a court expungement, whether they can do three cards in one visit, what each costs, whether payment must be in cash, and what identification to bring. These are not the same as the fingerprints taken for a Highway Patrol criminal-history search and you do not need to buy a criminal record to get them. One card is filed with the court, one is sent by the clerk to the Missouri Criminal Record Repository with the summons, and one is yours to keep. Start this early: it is a physical dependency people discover too late.",
            "Obtain Missouri Department of Revenue driver record. Order your Missouri driver record. It shows the offense classification and whether a commercial driver licence was ever issued, and commercial licence status at the time of arrest is an outright bar on the moving-violation ground."
          ],
          "actual": "Instructions request one standard fingerprint card and generic criminal history; no three-card procurement/distribution guidance and no Missouri DOR driver record instruction for the qualifying-traffic fixture.",
          "repair": "Carry the adopted three-card procurement and distribution instructions; for qualifying-traffic require the DOR driver record to check offense classification and CDL status at arrest. Do not fabricate cards or agency attestations."
        },
